index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..85ca209b181d706eaa6b5272a50126e3ac814e70
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/gguf-mxfp8-prefill.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# Experimental MXFP8 GGUF prefill
+
+Set `NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8=1` before starting the process to enable this
+explicit, lossy numerical profile. Unset or `0` retains the existing q8_1 path.
+The switch is immutable after its first query and must precede workspace planning.
+Use `NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4=0` when qualifying FP8 alone. The stored model
+weights and selected KV representation are unchanged.
+
+## Supported calls and routes
+
+The experiment supports an sm120 image on compute capability 12.x, positive K
+divisible by 256, and IQ3_XXS, IQ3_S, IQ2_XXS, IQ2_XS, IQ2_S, IQ4_XS, Q2_K and
+Q4_K. Unsupported devices/formats and calls below 256 columns retain the existing
+route. Supported decode/verification batches are at most 128 columns and remain
+on q8_1. Prefill errors can still affect later KV/GDN state and generated output.
+
+- At 256 through 1023 columns, a fused 128-row by 128-column tile uses producer
+  warps with cp.async staging and native block-scaled E4M3 MMA consumer warps.
+  Results pass directly through the existing store, residual or gate epilogue.
+- At 1024 columns and above, a bounded weight image feeds cuBLASLt. GEMM
+  accumulation and output are FP32, followed by the existing epilogue/BF16 cast.
+
+This width/type gate is a support rule, not a measured profitability rule for
+every device and matrix shape. There is no per-device FP8-tile/Q8-matrix selector
+in this implementation. The existing device profiles for other kernels remain
+separate. In particular, support for FP8 does not prove that FP8 is faster.
+
+## Numerical and resource boundaries
+
+Activations, after their optional column gather, and decoded FP32 weights use
+one E4M3 representation and one UE8M0 power-of-two scale per 32 values. The scale
+is `2^ceil(log2(amax/448))`, clamped to the finite UE8M0 range. All-zero groups use
+scale one. The encoder uses round-to-nearest-even and finite saturation.
+
+The five grid i-quants decode raw selectors through lookup entries carrying the
+actual maximum selector. This preserves actual per-group amax, signed scales
+and direct FP32-to-E4M3 rounding. Other supported types retain their FP32 value
+decoder. There is no FP16 weight intermediate or type-range-bound replacement.
+MMA accumulates in FP32. Dynamic shared-memory attributes are initialized per
+CUDA device; this is independent of the runtime stream or CUDA Graph.
+
+All activation, scale, padded-output, fallback and weight-image storage is
+caller-owned and included in workspace planning. The cuBLASLt weight image is
+capped at 64 MiB except for a minimum 128-row tile, rather than a full-model FP8
+copy. Its larger slab and FP32 output plane cost more transient storage than
+the historical 8 MiB implementation. Tile-only plans do not reserve an unused
+cuBLASLt slab. cuBLASLt plans are cached per device and geometry.
+
+The enabled Qwen prefill signature and all-family snapshot binding identify
+`mxfp8-e4m3-e8m0-f32-tile-v1`. Default signatures are unchanged. State from a
+different numerical profile must not be treated as interchangeable.
+
+## Qualification and use
+
+Independent CPU packed-GGUF decoders, a CPU E4M3 encoder and naive FP64 products
+qualify represented operands, including gathers, tails, extreme scales, stores,
+residual/gated epilogues, graph replay and a large slab boundary. Encoded-operand
+accuracy does not measure the quantization loss against the original model;
+model perplexity and request behavior are separate acceptance evidence.
+
+```powershell
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_MXFP8 = '1'
+$env:NINFER_GGUF_PREFILL_NVFP4 = '0'
+.\ninfer-serve.exe MODEL.ninfer --prefill-chunk 256
+```
+
+Restart with MXFP8 set to `0` to use q8_1. This remains default-off and
+experimental. The former two-pass-only 8 MiB implementation and its timings
+are historical, and do not describe this fused-tile implementation.
+
+The pipeline is adapted from `2-com-org/ninfer-5060-qwen` at
+`08c4fb70bec11063cae42eafe1c1b0dc3a7f993e`. Local actual-amax scaling, FP32
+interpretation and output boundaries differ from that repository's optimized
+scale-bound and some FP16/BF16 paths. Its numerical and performance results
+cannot substitute for qualification of this implementation.
